.TH YTNEFPROCESS 1 "" "ytnef" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ytnefprocess \- replace TNEF attachments in a mail message with their contents
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ytnefprocess
.RI < message
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ytnefprocess
reads a MIME mail message on standard input, unpacks every
.I application/ms-tnef
part with
.BR ytnef (1),
and writes the message to standard output with the extracted files attached
in place of the TNEF part. It works as a
.BR procmail (1)
filter, for example:
.PP
.nf
.RS
:0Bfw
* Content-Type:.*application/ms-tnef.*
| /usr/bin/ytnefprocess
.RE
.fi
.PP
It needs the Perl modules MIME::Parser, MIME::Entity (MIME-tools) and
Mail::Mailer (MailTools), and keeps temporary files under
.IR ~/.ytnef .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ytnef (1),
.BR procmail (1)
.SH HOMEPAGE
https://github.com/Yeraze/ytnef
